{"title":"Functions","markdown":{"headingText":"Functions","headingAttr":{"id":"sec-08_func","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n## Concepts and intutions {.unnumbered}\nFor most of us, hearing a function is traumatizing.\nStudying and is, we have a set of procedures.\nI think it is a part of the education failure.\n1- by reducing to monkey\n2- by breaking the a function and its visulization.\n\n\nWell, you actually use functions everyday, and it is a.\nthe major difference is that we do it a less quantitative way.\nSo if I take X decision, I get Y and if I take not X then I get not Y.\n\nIf one works X hours then I get Y money, well that's the theory and so it is not as neat as in mathematics.\n\nWell so why the complicated functions, well, they serve another purpose.\nAnd that is not the purpose of this chapter nor this book.\nIntuitively, we just need to that if we give an input then we get an output.\nIn fact, we want to unravel the relationship, infer what kind of functions is there.\nAnd ironically, the most popular one is just y =  a x+ b. So secondary school map.\n\n\n## Formal {.unnumbered}\nWe need three components to define a function, the starting and ending sets and the actual mapping.\nIt is written like f: X -> Y , x, y = f(x)\n\nAnd that's it. In general, there are unique so that f(x), this is called explicity.\nThis is different from implicit but also stochastic stuff.\n\nWell, X could be multidimensional or qualitative etc.\n\n## Examples {.unnumbered}\nThe traditional is y = a x + b.\n\nUsing integer Cnp is a function.\n\nBaker's ratio or making a cake.\n\nBut the shopping is another example: how much you spend.\n\n## Tips and warning {.unnumbered}\nWith any programming language, you can do 2 in one line.\nLife is not perfect and the explicit y = f(x) is a wishful thinking.\nIn fact, y = f(x1,x2,x3...)\nIn principle, one input leads to one output\nDummy variable\n\n## if you want to know more {.unnumbered}\n","srcMarkdow